\description{
Read the scans of a spectra file: every scan's header always, and its peak arrays only on request.

The many-files form of \code{\link{readers_read_spectra}}: every file read by one bridge process,
\code{threads} at a time, into one scan table - so a study's runs can be compared by instrument and
acquisition time from \code{files} without a loop.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_read_batch}. \code{records} begins with \code{source_index} (1-based, into \code{paths}) and
  \code{source_path}, then the columns of \code{\link{readers_read_spectra}}: \code{retention_time} in minutes;
  \code{injection_time} in ms; \code{total_ion_current} and \code{selected_ion_intensity} in the instrument's
  intensity units; \code{peak_count} in peaks; \code{compensation_voltage} in volts;
  \code{selected_ion_charge_state_guess} a charge; \code{scan_window_lower_mz}, \code{scan_window_upper_mz},
  \code{isolation_mz}, \code{isolation_width}, \code{selected_ion_mz} and \code{selected_ion_monoisotopic_guess_mz}
  in m/z; and with \code{peaks = TRUE} the list columns \code{mz} (m/z) and \code{intensity}.
  \code{files} has one row per input: \code{scan_count} in scans, \code{record_count} in scans after the
  \code{ms_order} filter, the run's \code{instrument_model}, \code{instrument_model_accession},
  \code{instrument_serial_number}, \code{acquisition_start_time} and \code{acquisition_start_time_is_utc}
  (flattened from each file's \code{source}; \code{NA} where the file does not record them), \code{caveats}
  and the error columns. \code{file_count}, \code{read_count} and \code{failed_count} count files;
  \code{record_count} and \code{returned_count} count scans over the files read; \code{row_count} counts the
  rows of \code{records}.

}
